{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/workroom implementation at exact clean pushed head 139b54fcfe9a8be641ed1c3eab66985bdeeec925 on request/dated-active-cause-v2, fulfilling planner's 2906cb7e under promise 60bdd5ee. Recut on main d91fb8b6.\n\nTHE DEFECT I WOULD HAVE SHIPPED, AND IT WAS MINE TWICE. worldCauseAtOrBefore stopped at the first retired artifact basis and never descended past it, while staleness() inherits the date THROUGH retired artifacts. The walks were not the same rule; the fold's was a strict subset, so the receipt boundary could admit what the CLI refused. The implementer authors an interposed artifact and supersedes it after the verdict, and the older pre-verdict cause beneath it goes invisible -- signer-controllable, no cooperation needed. This is the same defect as the break codex found in staleness(), in a second place, introduced by me while fixing the first.\n\nTestAnInterposedRetirementDoesNotHideAnOlderCauseFromTheReceipt pins it: restoring the continue fails it by name with 'an interposed post-verdict retirement hid an older pre-verdict cause, and the receipt took cross-author retirement authority'. Nothing in the tree caught it before.\n\nBOTH RECEIPT GUARDS ARE NOW INDIVIDUALLY COVERED. They were not: every receipt test refused through the co-signed path, so neutering the primary check left the whole package green. TestADirectReceiptRefusesWhenOnlyThePrimaryArtifactWasAlreadyStale isolates it with a healthy co-signed member, and fails by name when that check is neutered.\n\nBOTH AGGREGATION SEAMS ARE COVERED, each by a different test: per-target earliest by the withdrawal test, cross-basis by the order test, which now asserts the VALUE and not only stability -- taking the latest cause is also order-stable and still admits a merge the reviewer had already been shown.\n\nactiveRetirements is built once and passed to reviewedPathsWith rather than rebuilt per receipt and per co-signed basis; a measured review put the previous shape at roughly twice the fold cost. Its Verdict check is dropped as unreachable: effectiveSup is only written for records already ruled effective, so it read as a guard while guarding nothing.\n\nDEPLOYMENT ORDER: ProfileVersion is workroom-fold@10. Restart the resident and every adapter on the new binary BEFORE rebuilding gs. gofmt clean over every tracked Go file, go vet ./... clean, go test -count=1 ./... pass, race on cmd/gs 159.390s and internal/workroom 12.243s, internal/docset pass in 50.171s, 83 UI tests pass with 0 failures, git diff --check clean, worktree clean, origin equals the head.","body":{"commit":"139b54fcfe9a8be641ed1c3eab66985bdeeec925","path":"internal/workroom"}}